{
  "name": "JSRunner",
  "params": {
    "jsPath": "js/smAgent.js",
    "jobParams": {
      "repo": "epam/dmtools-dart",
      "maxTriggeredWorkflows": 3,
      "rules": [
        {
          "description": "RULE ORDER (dmtools-agents#682, live fa#1202/#1203 2026-10-03 23:05–23:57, still reproducing 2026-10-04 06:21–06:22): runs FIRST, ahead of merge-validated AND sweep-stale-validating (whose relative order is a documented #637 invariant — this rule preserves it by prefixing, never interleaving). A cancelled required check is never a verdict: the sweep skips cancelled conclusions by design and fail-validation owns red, so this rule cannot fight them — it never touches labels and never dispatches workflows, it only re-runs GitHub Actions runs. GitHub PR: armed (ai_validating) or latched (ai_validated) head whose REQUIRED check contexts (rule.requiredContexts, branch protection here: static/gate/agents-gate; in fa the kicker's sm-liveness/head-completeness) concluded CANCELLED — the kicker cancel-loop death: every silent-refresh push queued a new kicker run and the pending one was superseded (cancelled) in the shared concurrency group, required contexts died CANCELLED on fresh heads, PRs BLOCKED until manual reruns (2 dead zones + 2 manual reruns on 2026-10-03 alone). CANCELLED is read with branch-protection semantics: the LATEST check run per context is the verdict — a stale cancel under a fresh green re-stamp does NOT act (#695 review fix). NOT failure — failure paths exist; NOT pending-with-active-runs — the localAction probes every run on the head (hasActiveDispatchedRun pattern widened to all events) and skips while anything is in flight. localAction rerun_cancelled_checks re-runs (gh run rerun) the latest attempt-1 cancelled run per required context and posts a once-per-head marker comment citing the evidence — ONLY when the rerun set covers every cancelled context (a partial set defers the marker so the uncovered contexts stay actionable; #695). BEHIND (silent-update refreshes the head) and DIRTY (conflict-rework owns it) are excluded, and agent:rework defers to the rework leg. limit 2: the observed death takes two PRs per wave (fa#1202+#1203 in one 36-second push wave).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating",
              "ai_validated"
            ],
            "notLabels": [
              "agent:rework"
            ],
            "notMergeState": [
              "BEHIND",
              "DIRTY"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "rerun_cancelled_checks",
          "requiredContexts": [
            "static",
            "gate",
            "agents-gate"
          ],
          "limit": 2,
          "id": "rerun-cancelled-checks"
        },
        {
          "description": "Validated-but-stale: armed (ai_validating) + validation concluded but BASE MOVED (BEHIND only). BLOCKED must NOT unarm: since #483 BLOCKED is a real verdict, and on a freshly armed head BLOCKED simply means 'required checks pending' — unarming there races validate-armed in the SAME tick and deadlocks the PR forever (live: fa pr-762 armed at 08:25:37, unarmed 08:25:58 by the BLOCKED match, re-armed next tick, loop). silent-update-behind excludes ai_validating and merge-validated needs CLEAN, so without this unarm a genuinely moved base still deadlocks (live: fa pr-744) — BEHIND-only keeps that recovery and stops the self-inflicted one.",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "mergeState": [
              "BEHIND"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "unarm_validation",
          "limit": 1,
          "id": "unarm-stale-validation"
        },
        {
          "description": "RULE ORDER (dmtools-agents#637 aftermath, live fa pr-1174 2026-10-03): this rule MUST run before sweep-stale-validating — the 15-min staleness sweep eats every arm before the merge can consume it whenever the tick cadence slips past 15 min (night kicker slippage), looping arm→sweep→arm on a green merge-ready head. GitHub PR: validation green + CLEAN -> squash-merge (merge_pr verifies the sticky pr_approved latch on the PR; an un-approved green head latches ai_validated instead — see merge_pr). FIFO drain (#687).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "checks": "green",
            "mergeState": "CLEAN"
          },
          "localAction": "merge_pr",
          "limit": 1,
          "id": "merge-validated"
        },
        {
